Input: {"question": "When was the Turkish Republican Party founded?", "original_source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0136-96a8a5699dcf:d00", "start": 0, "end": 217, "text": "Republican Party (Turkey) Republican Party () was a former political party in Turkey Republican People’s party (CHP) which is usually credited as the founder of Turkish republic in 1923 was the oldest party in Turkey."}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0136-96a8a5699dcf:d00", "start": 218, "end": 343, "text": "But after the party adopted the policy of so-called left of center in the 1960s, two groups of MPs broke away from the party."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0136-96a8a5699dcf:d00", "start": 344, "end": 395, "text": "The first group in 1967 founded the Reliance Party."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0136-96a8a5699dcf:d00", "start": 396, "end": 453, "text": "Republican Party was founded by the second group in 1972."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0136-96a8a5699dcf:d00", "start": 454, "end": 496, "text": "The party was founded on 4 September 1972."}, "D1S6": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0136-96a8a5699dcf:d00", "start": 497, "end": 566, "text": "The chairman of the Party was Kemal Satır, an ex vice prime minister."}, "D1S7": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0136-96a8a5699dcf:d00", "start": 567, "end": 570, "text": "But"}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0136-96a8a5699dcf:d01", "start": 0, "end": 503, "text": "Philadelphia ) : Willkie / McNary primaries 1944 ( Chicago ) : Dewey / Bricker primaries 1948 ( Philadelphia ) : Dewey / Warren primaries 1952 ( Chicago ) : Eisenhower / Nixon primaries 1956 ( San Francisco ) : Eisenhower / Nixon primaries 1960 ( Chicago ) : Nixon / Lodge primaries 1964 ( San Francisco ) : Goldwater / Miller primaries 1968 ( Miami Beach ) : Nixon / Agnew primaries 1972 ( Miami Beach ) : Nixon / Agnew primaries 1976 ( Kansas City ) : Ford / Dole primaries 1980 ( Detroit ) : Reagan /"}, "D3S1": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0136-96a8a5699dcf:d02", "start": 0, "end": 450, "text": "Party ( 1988–94 ) Greens Party ( YP ) ( 2008–12 ) Justice Party ( AP ) ( 1961–1980 ) Liberal Republican Party ( SCF ) ( 1995 ) Liberty Party ( HP ) ( 1955–58 ) Motherland Party ( ANAP ) ( 1983–2009 ) Nation Party ( MP ) ( 1948–53 ) Nation Party ( MP ) ( 1962–77 ) National Development Party ( MKP ) ( 1945–58 ) National Order Party ( MNP ) ( 1970–71 ) National Salvation Party ( MSP ) ( 1972–81 ) National Women's Party of Turkey ( TUKP ) ( 1972–81 )"}, "D4S1": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0136-96a8a5699dcf:d03", "start": 0, "end": 120, "text": "Republican Turkish Party The Republican Turkish Party (, CTP) is a social-democratic political party in Northern Cyprus."}, "D4S2": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0136-96a8a5699dcf:d03", "start": 121, "end": 253, "text": "The party was founded in 1970 by Ahmet Mithat Berberoğlu, a lawyer, in opposition to the leadership of Fazıl Küçük and Rauf Denktaş."}, "D4S3": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0136-96a8a5699dcf:d03", "start": 254, "end": 441, "text": "On 30 June 2008, the Republican Turkish Party became a consultative member of the Socialist International (voted in by all members except the Greek Cypriot Movement for Social Democracy)."}, "D4S4": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0136-96a8a5699dcf:d03", "start": 442, "end": 494, "text": "It became a full member of the organization in 2014."}, "D4S5": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0136-96a8a5699dcf:d03", "start": 495, "end": 599, "text": "The CTP is a social democratic political party, positioned on the centre-left on the political spectrum."}, "D4S6": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0136-96a8a5699dcf:d03", "start": 600, "end": 631, "text": "The party espoused a pro-Soviet"}, "D5S1": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0136-96a8a5699dcf:d04", "start": 0, "end": 61, "text": "office , but was unable to pass major Square Deal proposals ."}, "D5S2": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0136-96a8a5699dcf:d04", "start": 62, "end": 209, "text": "He did succeed in naming his successor , Secretary of War William Howard Taft , who easily defeated Bryan again in the 1908 presidential election ."}, "D5S3": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0136-96a8a5699dcf:d04", "start": 210, "end": 302, "text": "[ 65 ] By 1907 , Roosevelt identified himself with the left-center of the Republican Party ."}, "D5S4": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0136-96a8a5699dcf:d04", "start": 303, "end": 534, "text": "[ 66 ] He explained his balancing act : Again and again in my public career I have had to make head against mob spirit , against the tendency of poor , ignorant and turbulent people who feel a rancorous jealousy and hatred of those"}}, "original_cards": [{"doc_id": "ramdocs-0136-96a8a5699dcf:d00", "card_id": "ramdocs-0136-96a8a5699dcf:d00:c0", "entity": "Republican Party", "scope": "Turkey", "claim": "The Republican Party was founded on 4 September 1972.", "answer": "4 September 1972", "quote": "Republican Party was founded by the second group in 1972. The party was founded on 4 September 1972.", "original_document_number": 1}, {"doc_id": "ramdocs-0136-96a8a5699dcf:d03", "card_id": "ramdocs-0136-96a8a5699dcf:d03:c0", "entity": "Republican Turkish Party", "scope": "founding date", "claim": "The Republican Turkish Party was founded in 1970.", "answer": "1970", "quote": "The party was founded in 1970 by Ahmet Mithat Berberoğlu, a lawyer, in opposition to the leadership of Fazıl Küçük and Rauf Denktaş.", "original_document_number": 4}], "current_answers": ["4 September 1972", "1970"], "candidate_answers": [{"candidate_id": "R0", "answer": "4 September 1972", "origin": "initial"}, {"candidate_id": "R1", "answer": "1970", "origin": "initial"}]}

